OL,3,GNEWSAHome secretary to hear voters'
OL,4,Aimmigration views
OL,5,
OL,6,FA group of Tyneside voters have been
OL,7,Fpromised their views on immigration
OL,8,Fwill be put to the home secretary after
OL,9,Fthey took part in a panel advising MPs.
OL,11,FAbout 25 people from the area were
OL,12,Fasked by the Home Affairs Committee to
OL,13,Flook at the number of migrant workers
OL,14,Fthe UK needed.
OL,16,FAnd one panel member from North Shields
OL,17,Fgot a chance to challenge political
OL,18,Fleaders as the findings were revealed
OL,19,Fat Westminster.
OL,23,APub: 12-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,397,390,260,160,0,100
